From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: pass the AP_VLAN interface to sta_set_4addr under NSS offload

With the NSS Wi-Fi offload ath11k keeps a 4-address station on an AP_VLAN
interface of its own, an ext vdev in the NSS firmware, and sets it up
from the sta_set_4addr callback, which it recognizes by the interface
type. ieee80211_change_station() hands drv_sta_set_4addr() the AP_VLAN
for that reason (235-001), but drv_sta_set_4addr() maps every AP_VLAN
back to its AP with get_bss_sdata(). The driver only ever saw the AP
interface, so the ext vdev was created and never configured or brought
up, and no frame passed to or from a WDS station.

Skip the mapping with SUPPORTS_NSS_OFFLOAD, as 235-001 already does in
drv_sta_add() and drv_sta_rate_tbl_update().

Link: https://github.com/kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma/issues/87
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
@@ -1699,7 +1699,11 @@ static inline void drv_sta_set_4addr(str
 				     struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 				     struct ieee80211_sta *sta, bool enabled)
 {
-	sdata = get_bss_sdata(sdata);
+	/* The NSS offload keeps a 4-address station on its own AP_VLAN
+	 * interface in the driver, so the driver has to see that interface.
+	 */
+	if (!ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_NSS_OFFLOAD))
+		sdata = get_bss_sdata(sdata);
 
 	might_sleep();
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(local->hw.wiphy);
